  "description" = 'SEC Form 4 open-market purchases (code P, common/ordinary shares) evaluated over 2016-01-01 to 2026-03-31 (IS through 2024-03-31; 24-month OOS 2024-04-01 to 2026-03-31, 502 sessions). Source: SEC quarterly Form 3/4/5 datasets (284,580 code-P buys). Delay: Form 4 is due within 2 business days; entry at the next trading day open after FILING_DATE. Equal-weight 10-slot portfolio in excess of SPY at 10 bps/side base cost (0 and 20 bps stress). Pre-registered primary variant cluster-3p-10d (>= 3 distinct reporting-owner groups within 10 calendar days, H=20): 468 full-sample trades (+0.31% excess CAGR, Sharpe +0.083, max DD -40.78%), 79 OOS events (below 100-event bar), OOS excess CAGR +7.33%, OOS excess Sharpe +0.977 (+0.868 at 20 bps), DSR 0.351 < 0.95 (N=12). FreeStockAlerts confirmation-baseline (H=20): 680 trades (OOS 139 events, OOS excess Sharpe -0.823). Verdict: no-edge (failed OOS event count and DSR bars). Limits: daily bars cover 468 of the 600 pre-registered tickers (Yahoo Finance has no history for 132 delisted, acquired or renamed issuers, so the result has survivorship bias; 189,879 rows are in tickers without bars), price guard on the as-traded close (618 rows rejected), post-2023 Rule 10b5-1 checkbox regime break (sensitivity OOS Sharpe +0.823, 75 events), underlying equity study only (live Vertex rules require defined-risk options). Spec: docs/specs/strategies/insider-purchase-confirmation.md. Research only.',
